## General

### What is Revela?

Revela is a static site generator built specifically for photographers. It takes your photos and generates a fast, beautiful portfolio website with no database and no server, just HTML and optimized images.

### Do I need programming experience?

No. Revela runs as a simple text menu that you control with the arrow keys and <kbd>Enter</kbd>, and a setup wizard guides you through creating your first site. You'll need to be comfortable with basic file management (creating folders, copying files), but no coding is required. [Your First Site](../../docs/get-started/first-site/) walks you through it in six steps.

### Is my website online as soon as Revela has built it?

No. Revela builds the website on your computer, in the `output` folder; it isn't an online service and needs no account. To put the site online, you upload that folder to a web host of your choice. The [Deployment guide](../../docs/guide/deployment/) shows free options such as GitHub Pages, Netlify and Cloudflare Pages.

### Does Revela change my original photos?

No. Revela only reads the photos in your `source` folder and writes separate web versions into `output`. Your originals are never resized, re-saved or moved.

### What platforms does Revela run on?

Windows (x64 and ARM64), macOS (Apple Silicon), and Linux (x64 and ARM64). Every [download](../downloads/) is a ready-to-run program, so there's no runtime installation needed.

### Does Revela require Node.js, Ruby, or Python?

No. The Standalone and Full [downloads](../downloads/) are self-contained programs with nothing else to install. Only the optional .NET global tool needs the .NET 10 SDK; its `.nupkg` files are attached to each [GitHub Release](https://github.com/Spectara/Revela/releases) (Revela is not on NuGet.org yet).

---

## Images

### Which files can I put in?

JPEG, PNG, WebP and GIF. RAW files are not read, so export JPEGs from Capture One, Lightroom or your photo editor first, ideally at full resolution in Display P3 or Adobe RGB. See [exporting from your photo editor](../../docs/guide/images/#exporting-from-your-photo-editor) for a recommended preset.

### What image formats does Revela generate?

Revela generates **AVIF**, **WebP**, and **JPEG**: modern formats for maximum compression, with fallbacks for older browsers. Each image is generated in multiple sizes for responsive loading.

### How many sizes are generated per image?

The theme decides. The built-in Lumina theme defines 160, 320, 480, 640, 720, 960, 1280, 1440, 1920, and 2560 pixels. Revela generates every theme size that is smaller than your original, plus one version at the original size for full-screen viewing. Nothing is ever upscaled.

### How fast is image processing?

Revela uses **NetVips** (libvips) and processes several photos in parallel. Builds are incremental: only new or changed photos are processed again. The first build of a large collection still takes a while, because every photo is turned into several sizes in AVIF, WebP and JPEG. As an example, about 1,200 full-resolution photos took around half an hour on a 6-core server; later builds took seconds to minutes, depending on how much changed.

### What EXIF data is preserved?

By default, EXIF data is **stripped** from generated images (for privacy and file size). The original EXIF data is read during scanning for statistics, sorting, and filtering, but it isn't embedded in the output.

